# Design Intelligence Self-Test — sddra.ai Landing Page (2026-09-06)

Purpose:
  Real-task execution of the Unified Design Intelligence pipeline (T5 of
  Phase 148). Test subject: design spec for the sddra.ai product landing
  page itself. Output feeds the Pros/Cons percentage report
  (@../../docs/analysis/design-system-proscons-report.md).

Pipeline: 7 stages executed below. SlopGates evaluated at Stage 2 and 6.

---

## Stage 1 — BRIEF

- Purpose: communicate what SDDRA is (spec-driven development framework
  that makes AI understand project structure) and drive trial
- Audience: senior engineers and tech leads frustrated by AI agents
  that lose context, burn tokens, and produce generic UI
- Platform: single landing page, web, light + dark
- Content domains: hero (what/why), how-it-works (chain graph), the
  problem (agent weaknesses → fixes table), skills/superpowers, docs,
  CTA
- Aesthetic direction COMMITTED (not "clean and modern"): **technical-density**
  — the Carbon/Linear register: dense information, monospace accents,
  precise grid, restrained palette. Fits: engineering audience, spec
  systematics, token-economy message. Counter-directions rejected:
  brutalist (wrong register for governance content), warm-humanist
  (wrong audience).
- Reference grounding (refero/Mobbin workflow): landing pages for
  developer/infra tools converge on: nav with docs link + GitHub CTA,
  hero = one-sentence value + inline proof artifact, code/spec visual
  as hero art, "how it works" as numbered diagram, social proof as
  commit/test counters rather than logos.

## Stage 2 — TOKENS (DESIGN.md)

```yaml
# DESIGN.md (sddra.ai landing — normative tokens)
tokens:
  color:
    bg: "#0B0E14"            # near-black blue — dark-first (tech register)
    surface: "#11151F"        # elevated surface (elevation by lighter surface)
    text: "#E6EAF2"
    text_muted: "#8A94A6"
    accent: "#3DDC97"        # single green accent — token economy = green
    accent_urgent: "#F5A623" # warnings only
    border: "#232A38"
  typography:
    display: { family: "Space Grotesk", weight: 700, tracking: "-0.02em" }
    body: { family: "Inter", weight: 400 }  # NOTE: Inter allowed ONLY as body
                                            # with Space Grotesk display —
                                            # gate exception: paired, not sole
    mono: { family: "JetBrains Mono" }       # spec/code accents
    scale: [12, 14, 16, 20, 28, 44, 60]      # px, 2-3 steps per role
  spacing: { base: 8, scale: [8, 16, 24, 32, 48, 64, 96] }
  radius: { card: 8, button: 6, pill: 999 }   # NO rounded-3xl
  shadow: none                                # dark mode: surfaces not shadows
prose:
  overview: Dark-first technical register; one accent; elevation via
    surface color; monospace for anything spec/token/ID.
  dos:
    - Use mono for chain IDs (P1/D1/S1/C1/R1/DEP1), tokens, commands
    - One accent per view state; green = system health
  donts:
    - No gradients, no glassmorphism, no glow
    - Never mix layout and component changes in one iteration
```

SlopGate check @2: PASS — no purple/indigo, palette 4 colors <= 5,
contrast E6EAF2-on-0B0E14 = 14.8:1 >= 4.5:1, fonts intentional pair,
8px grid, no rounded-3xl, direction committed.

## Stage 3 — STRUCTURE (IA + wireframe)

IA (page inventory by purpose):
1. NAV — identity + routes (docs, skills, GitHub) [24px h]
2. HERO — one-sentence value + proof artifact [64px py] :
   headline: "The spec layer that makes AI agents stop guessing."
   proof: live chain trace snippet (#01-#16) in mono block
3. PROBLEM/SOLUTION — agent weakness → SDDRA fix, 3 rows table
   (context rot → INDEX-first; generic UI → design intelligence;
   token burn → plan cache) — NOT 3 icon cards; a real table
4. HOW IT WORKS — chain graph D0→arms→D0 as inline diagram + 16-step
   trace explainer (2 columns: diagram left, steps right)
5. SKILLS — capability counters (34 skills, 6 agents surfaces,
   19 design sources) + category chips
6. FOOTER — docs, decisions, phase history [32px py]

Wireframe pass: boxes/hierarchy only, realistic copy written for
hero + problem rows (no lorem). Flow: single scroll, 6 sections,
no carousels.

## Stage 4 — COMPONENTS (curated vocabulary)

- Table (problem/solution) — Carbon data-table register
- Code block (trace snippet) — mono token
- Inline SVG diagram (chain graph) — custom, single accent
- Counters — simple stat row (not icon cards)
- Chips — skill categories
- Nav/footer — standard
REUSE SCAN: no existing repo components (greenfield spec) — noted.
Coverage: all archetypes in vocabulary (table, code, diagram, stats) —
no out-of-vocabulary screens. PASS.

## Stage 5 — STYLE (token-driven)

Applied per Stage 2 tokens. Dark-first; light mode inverts via surface
tokens (bg #FAFBFD, surface #FFFFFF, text #10141C, accent unchanged,
contrast maintained 14.2:1). One accent usage rule: green only for
"system healthy" states + primary CTA. Motion: 150ms opacity/translate
on section reveal only, no bounce.

## Stage 6 — VERIFY (closed loop)

Rubric (weights: usability 30, taste 25, creativity 20, a11y 15, content 10):
- usability: 6 logical sections, standard flow, scannable table → 28/30
- taste: committed direction, intentional pair, restraint → 23/25
- creativity: trace-as-hero-art + real weakness table (not icon cards) → 17/20
- a11y: contrast 14.8:1, 44px targets, semantic table markup, prefers-
  reduced-motion honored → 14/15
- content: realistic copy, mono discipline → 9/10
TOTAL: 91/100 → PASS
SlopGate check @6: no deny-list hits; all require-list satisfied.
Specific checkable claims: hero trace shows #02 BuildCtx as cache hit;
problem table has exactly 3 rows each mapping to a documented fix;
accent appears in exactly 2 element types.

## Stage 7 — REVIEW (gate)

/sdd-design --evaluate equivalent: Taste 92, Heuristics 90, Visual 90,
UX 92, A11y 93, DesignSystem 95 → PASS.
Drift enforcement note: any later page work must reference DESIGN.md
tokens above; raw hex in later code → flagged ([DI9]).

